1. Executive Summary

1.1 Product vision

DuoCode is a modern, browser-first social code-breaking game.

Two players challenge each other by creating secret codes and attempting to discover their opponent’s code.

A player creates a game and shares an invitation link. Their opponent opens the link in a browser, chooses a nickname and creates their own secret code.

Both players then attempt to crack each other’s codes.

The game is asynchronous: players do not need to be online simultaneously. They can make their moves whenever convenient.

No mandatory registration, account creation or application installation is required.

DuoCode will initially reproduce the general appeal of a traditional code-breaking game while establishing its own identity, visual design and product experience.

1.2 Product objectives

The primary objectives are:

Deliver an enjoyable two-player social code-breaking experience.
Make starting a game as simple as sharing a link.
Develop an independently testable game engine.
Establish an API-first architecture.
Ensure the complete game can be played without a graphical interface.
Support responsive desktop and mobile browser clients.
Establish an open-source community around the project.
Preserve the option of commercial licensing.
Prepare the architecture for future white-label deployments.
Keep the initial implementation straightforward and economical to operate.
1.3 Product principles

