6.3 Logical architecture

The system shall be divided into the following logical components:

Game engine.
Game management service.
Player and invitation management.
Guess and feedback processing.
Results management.
REST API.
Persistence layer.
Automated testing and simulation tools.
The game engine shall have no dependency on Oak, HTTP or the database.

It must be independently executable and testable.

6.4 Stateless services

Application instances shall be stateless.

Game state and player information shall be persisted in PostgreSQL.

The architecture shall permit multiple application instances without requiring session affinity.

6.5 Database

PostgreSQL shall be the authoritative persistent store.

The initial logical data model shall include:

