The community licence shall permit use, modification and distribution, including commercial use, subject to AGPL requirements.

Where modified software is offered as a network service, the applicable source-code disclosure requirements of AGPL shall be respected.

13.3 Dual licensing

The architecture and ownership arrangements should preserve the possibility of offering a separate proprietary commercial licence.

Potential commercial licensing may permit:

Closed-source modifications.
Proprietary integrations.
Commercial white-label deployments.
Commercial hosted services without AGPL obligations applying to the separately licensed use.
