Mandatory design constraints

The first MVP is backend-only.
The complete game must be playable using curl or Postman.
The game engine must be independent of the API framework.
Feedback calculation must be independently verifiable.
PostgreSQL is the authoritative store.
Application services must be stateless.
API security must protect secret codes and player identities.
Automated simulation must use the public REST API.
Simulation must support deterministic replay.
OpenAPI 3.1 is the API contract.
AGPL-3.0-only is the intended community licence.
Future dual licensing must remain possible.
White-label capability is a future product objective and architectural constraint, not an MVP implementation requirement.
Original branding and visual design must be used.
