20. Closing Statement

DuoCode is intended to be a small, enjoyable social game built on a sound technical foundation.

The initial objective is deliberately modest: create a complete two-player game that works reliably through a REST API.

The project should demonstrate good engineering practices from the beginning, including independent game logic, automated testing, reproducible simulation, security and clear API contracts.

The architecture should leave room for future development without making the initial implementation unnecessarily complicated.

The long-term opportunity is to grow DuoCode from a simple social game into an extensible code-breaking platform, with community development, commercial licensing and potential white-label deployments.

Build the game first. Prove the engine. Validate the API. Then build the experience.


